      <h2>Why Everton Has Its Own Plumbing Reality</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Everton sits on the ridge above Liverpool city centre. The water tower is the local landmark. The area has changed more than any other part of Liverpool in the last decade. L5 property values are up 75% in five years.</p>

        <p>The new Everton FC stadium at Bramley-Moore Dock opened for the 2025/26 season. That's £5.5 billion of waterfront work around it. Project Jennifer on Great Homer Street brought a new district centre with Sainsbury's, B&M and the Greatie Market. The housing stock is changing too.</p>

        <p>What you find behind any front door in L5 could be 130-year-old Victorian pipework or push-fit plastic from 2015. We work on both every week.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <p>Everton is also one of 16 Liverpool wards covered by selective licensing. Every private rental needs a council licence. CP12 gas safety paperwork is part of the inspection. We do the paperwork to the standard the council expects.</p>

        <p>The buy-to-let market is the biggest in the city. L5 has the highest yield at 7.5%. That means lots of landlords, lots of HMOs, lots of students and healthcare workers renting near the three universities and Royal Liverpool Hospital. We cover them all at fixed rates.</p>
      </div>
