      <h2>While You Wait For Our Engineer</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Four steps to protect the home while we're on the way.</p>
      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">1</span><div><strong>Find the stopcock and turn it off</strong><p>For any water leak, the stopcock is your first move. In most Everton terraces it's under the kitchen sink or in the cellar. In new-build flats it's often in the airing cupboard. Turn it clockwise to stop all water.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">2</span><div><strong>If you smell gas, get out</strong><p>Don't touch any switches. Open windows as you leave. Call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Then us on <a href="tel:01515580334">0151 558 0334</a> once the home is safe.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">3</span><div><strong>No heating? Check the pressure gauge</strong><p>Look at the gauge on the boiler. It should sit between 1 and 1.5 bar. Below 0.5, you can top it up with the filling loop underneath. That fixes about half of all "no heating" calls. If it doesn't, call us.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">4</span><div><strong>Photograph the damage</strong><p>Take photos and video before you start cleaning. Insurance claims need proof. Landlords need this for selective licensing records. We give you our own fault report with photos as well.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

